# AWS Infrastructure Automation with Terraform & Ansible

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates AWS infrastructure automation using Terraform and Ansible.

Terraform is used to create the AWS VPC, subnet, security group, and EC2 instance. Ansible is used to configure the EC2 server and deploy Nginx.

## Technologies Used

- AWS
- Terraform
- Ansible
- EC2
- VPC
- Ubuntu Linux
- Nginx
- Git & GitHub

## Architecture

Terraform → VPC → Subnet → Security Group → EC2 → Ansible → Nginx → Web Application

## Project Workflow

1. Created AWS infrastructure using Terraform
2. Created custom VPC and networking components
3. Provisioned EC2 instance
4. Connected to EC2 using Ansible
5. Installed and configured Nginx
6. Deployed a custom web page

## Final Output

*Hello from Terraform and Ansible*

## What I Learned

- AWS VPC networking
- Infrastructure as Code with Terraform
- Terraform modules
- Ansible automation
- Linux server configuration
- Nginx deployment
